      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ATHREESHOTEAGLE (2) sets the benchmark after winning the NR up to 39 at Wagin, scoring from Sanford Bart and having LOWLANDS BEACH BOY (3) covered by 7.2m. His Bunbury third in an NR 40 to 54 the run prior gives that form some depth, with the return to 1823m the main query rather than his current condition. LOWLANDS BEACH BOY is the obvious danger. He must turn around that Wagin margin, but he is a Narrogin track-and-distance winner and gets a more favourable starting point than last week. STAR OF THE GALAXY (7) enters off a close Wagin third in an NR 40 to 55 and is a credible upset chance if he repeats that, though the second row and his plain Bunbury run before it keep him below the top pair. DANGER (8) resumes after five months and needs to improve on his well-beaten Northam eighth, but his previous fourth in a 2-4 Win and solid broader profile give him an each-way chance if he is forward enough first-up.",
